      "featured": true,
      "summary": "Brand guidelines for Spirit, an activewear and lifestyle clothing brand. 53 pages.",
      "overview": "Spirit makes clothing for training, recovery and everyday wear. We designed the full identity and a 53-page guideline book covering the logo, colour, type, imagery and how they are used on clothing, packaging, retail and digital.",
      "challenge": "Most activewear brands use loud logos and bright colours. Spirit wanted a calmer look that still works on sports kit, and that stays consistent from a hang tag to an app screen.",
      "solution": "The emblem is an S made from two continuous strokes, with a light, widely spaced SPIRIT wordmark. The palette is black, charcoal, graphite and white, and all type is set in Satoshi. The book covers logo construction, sizes and misuse, then shows the brand on t-shirts, tanks, bottles, yoga mats, bags, hang tags, boxes, a campaign, the website, an app and a smartwatch.",
